### 1. Introduction

Orion Manufacturing, Inc. (OMI) is committed to maintaining the highest standards of safety, quality, and efficiency in our manufacturing processes. This document outlines the policies, procedures, and protocols related to manufacturing safety, packaging, and distribution. It is designed to ensure compliance with industry regulations and to promote a culture of safety throughout the organization.

### 2. Definitions

- **Orion Manufacturing, Inc. (OMI):** A leading manufacturer of precision components based in Springfield, USA.
- **Personal Protective Equipment (PPE):** Equipment worn to minimize exposure to hazards that can cause serious workplace injuries and illnesses.
- **Safety Data Sheet (SDS):** A document that provides information on the properties of hazardous chemicals and how they affect health and safety in the workplace.
- **Quality Control (QC):** Measures implemented to ensure that the products meet specified quality standards.
- **Inventory Management System (IMS):** A software application that helps manage inventory levels, orders, sales, and deliveries.

### 3. Manufacturing Safety Policies

#### 3.1 Safety Training

All employees at OMI are required to complete safety training upon hiring and annually thereafter. Training will be conducted by the Safety and Compliance Department, led by Sarah Johnson, Safety Manager. The training will cover:

- Emergency response procedures
- Proper use of PPE
- Equipment operation safety

**Procedure:**  
- New hires must complete the Safety Orientation Program (SOP) within their first week.
- Annual refreshers will be scheduled, with participation tracked in the Learning Management System (LMS).

#### 3.2 Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)

OMI mandates the use of PPE in designated areas where hazards are present. This includes:

- Safety goggles
- Hard hats
- Hearing protection
- Steel-toed boots
- Respirators in specific areas of the facility

**Procedure:**  
- PPE will be issued by the Safety Department upon employee onboarding.
- Supervisors are responsible for enforcing PPE compliance in their respective departments.

#### 3.3 Hazard Communication

OMI follows the OSHA Hazard Communication Standard (HCS). All chemicals used in manufacturing must have an SDS available and properly labeled.

**Procedure:**  
- The Chemical Inventory System (CIS) must be updated quarterly by the Production Supervisor, Mark Thompson.
- SDS must be accessible to all employees in the central Safety Station located near the break room.

#### 3.4 Equipment Safety

All equipment must be inspected regularly to ensure safe operation. The Maintenance Department, led by James Rodriguez, is responsible for regular inspections and repairs.

**Procedure:**  
- A monthly equipment safety checklist will be maintained.
- Any equipment found defective must be reported immediately to the Maintenance Department.

### 4. Packaging Procedures

#### 4.1 Packaging Standards

All products must be packaged in compliance with OMI's packaging standards which align with industry norms. Packaging must ensure product integrity during transportation and storage.

**Procedure:**  
- The Packaging Engineering Team, headed by Lisa Chen, will review and approve all packaging designs.
- Each packaging batch will be tested for durability and compliance with ISO 9001 standards.

#### 4.2 Quality Control

Quality Control (QC) checks will be performed at various stages of the packaging process to ensure compliance with specifications.

**Procedure:**  
- QC inspectors will conduct checks at the end of each packaging line.
- Non-conforming products must be segregated and reported to the Quality Assurance Manager, Tom Baker.

#### 4.3 Environmental Considerations

OMI is committed to sustainable practices. Packaging materials should be recyclable and sourced from sustainable suppliers.

**Procedure:**  
- The Procurement Department, led by Nancy Davis, must prioritize vendors who provide eco-friendly packaging solutions.
- Annual reviews of packaging materials will be conducted to assess environmental impacts.

### 5. Distribution Protocols

#### 5.1 Transportation Safety

Safety during transportation is paramount. OMI uses third-party logistics providers for distribution and requires that they adhere to OMI's safety standards.

**Procedure:**  
- Transportation Safety Audits will be conducted bi-annually by the Logistics Coordinator, Brian Wilson.
- Drivers must complete a safety briefing before each route.

#### 5.2 Inventory Management

The Inventory Management System (IMS) must be used to track inventory levels and manage stock efficiently.

**Procedure:**  
- Daily inventory counts will be conducted by warehouse staff under the supervision of Warehouse Manager, Angela Lee.
- Discrepancies must be reported to the Inventory Control Specialist, Tim Green.

#### 5.3 Delivery Procedures

All deliveries must be scheduled and documented through the IMS. Customer service representatives will confirm delivery details with clients.

**Procedure:**  
- Delivery schedules will be communicated to the production floor to ensure product availability.
- Customers must be informed of delivery times at least 24 hours in advance.

### 6. Compliance and Auditing

OMI will conduct regular audits to ensure compliance with safety, packaging, and distribution policies. The Compliance Officer, Rachel Adams, will oversee these audits.

**Procedure:**  
- Audits will occur quarterly, with findings reported to the executive team.
- Non-compliance issues must be addressed within 30 days.

### 7. Roles and Responsibilities

- **Safety Manager (Sarah Johnson):** Oversees all safety training and compliance.
- **Production Supervisor (Mark Thompson):** Ensures compliance with safety and quality standards on the production floor.
- **Quality Assurance Manager (Tom Baker):** Responsible for maintaining product quality and compliance with standards.
- **Logistics Coordinator (Brian Wilson):** Manages transportation safety and delivery scheduling.
- **Warehouse Manager (Angela Lee):** Oversees inventory management and warehouse operations.
- **Procurement Department (Nancy Davis):** Responsible for sourcing materials that meet environmental standards.

### 8. Emergency Procedures

In the event of an emergency, such as a fire or chemical spill, the following procedures must be followed:

- **Evacuation Plan:** All employees must evacuate to the designated assembly area located at the north parking lot.
- **Emergency Contacts:** Internal emergency contacts include the Safety Manager (Sarah Johnson) and the Facility Manager (Henry Black).
- **First Aid:** First Aid Kits are located throughout the facility. Trained first responders are available on-site.

### 9. Conclusion

Orion Manufacturing, Inc. is dedicated to maintaining a safe and efficient manufacturing environment. This policy document serves as a comprehensive guide for all employees regarding manufacturing safety, packaging, and distribution procedures. Compliance with these procedures is vital for the safety of our employees and the quality of our products. Regular reviews and updates will ensure that OMI remains at the forefront of industry standards.

**End of Document**

### 10. Training and Development

Continuous training and development are critical components of Orion Manufacturing, Inc.'s (OMI) commitment to safety, quality, and operational efficiency. OMI will provide regular training sessions for all employees to ensure they are equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge to perform their jobs safely and effectively.

**Training Programs:**

- **Safety Training:** All employees will undergo an initial safety training program during their onboarding process, with refresher courses held annually. This training will cover emergency procedures, proper equipment handling, and hazard recognition.
  
  **Procedure:**
  - New hires must complete the safety training program within the first week of employment.
  - Refresher courses will be scheduled quarterly and attendance will be mandatory.

- **Operational Training:** Employees will receive training specific to their roles, such as machinery operation, quality control processes, and inventory management systems.

  **Procedure:**
  - Each department head is responsible for identifying training needs and coordinating with the Training Coordinator, Lisa Martinez, to develop and implement specialized training programs.
  - Training effectiveness will be evaluated through assessments and performance reviews.

- **Leadership Development:** OMI encourages leadership development through mentorship programs and management training for aspiring leaders within the organization.

  **Procedure:**
  - Interested employees may apply for the Leadership Development Program, which will be reviewed by the HR Manager, David Chen.
  - Participants will be paired with mentors from senior management and will engage in monthly training workshops.

### 11. Communication Protocols

Effective communication is essential for maintaining safety, quality, and efficiency within OMI. Clear communication channels will be established to ensure that all employees are informed of relevant updates, policies, and changes.

**Communication Methods:**

- **Weekly Team Meetings:** Departments will hold weekly meetings to discuss ongoing projects, safety updates, and any challenges faced.

  **Procedure:**
  - Each team leader will prepare an agenda and distribute it to team members at least one day prior to the meeting.
  - Meeting minutes will be documented and shared in a common drive accessible to all team members.

- **Digital Communication Tools:** OMI will utilize digital tools such as Slack and Microsoft Teams for real-time communication among employees.

  **Procedure:**
  - Employees are required to join relevant channels and participate actively to foster collaboration and information sharing.
  - Important announcements will also be posted in a dedicated announcements channel to ensure visibility.

- **Feedback Mechanism:** A structured feedback system will be implemented to encourage employees to share suggestions or report concerns.

  **Procedure:**
  - Employees can submit feedback through an anonymous online form available on the company intranet.
  - The HR department will review submitted feedback monthly and present it at the executive team meetings for consideration.

### 12. Environmental Sustainability

OMI is committed to implementing environmentally sustainable practices throughout its operations. This includes reducing waste, conserving resources, and ensuring compliance with environmental regulations.

**Sustainability Initiatives:**

- **Waste Reduction Programs:** OMI will establish recycling programs in all departments and promote waste reduction strategies among employees.

  **Procedure:**
  - Recycling bins will be placed in strategic locations throughout the facility, and employees will receive training on proper waste segregation.
  - Monthly reports on waste reduction efforts will be compiled by the Environmental Compliance Officer, Rebecca Foster.

- **Energy Efficiency Measures:** OMI will invest in energy-efficient machinery and practices to minimize its carbon footprint.

  **Procedure:**
  - The Facilities Manager, Henry Black, will conduct annual assessments of energy use and identify areas for improvement.
  - Employees will be encouraged to adopt energy-saving practices, such as turning off equipment when not in use.

- **Sustainable Sourcing:** The Procurement Department, led by Nancy Davis, will prioritize sourcing materials from environmentally responsible suppliers.

  **Procedure:**
  - Suppliers will be evaluated based on their sustainability practices, and preference will be given to those who demonstrate a commitment to reducing environmental impact.
  - A sustainability report will be generated annually to assess the effectiveness of sourcing practices and identify opportunities for further improvement.

### 13. Conclusion

Orion Manufacturing, Inc. is dedicated to fostering a culture of safety, quality, and environmental responsibility. This policy document, which includes comprehensive guidelines for training, communication, and sustainability initiatives, serves as a roadmap for all employees to follow. Adherence to these policies will not only enhance the safety and efficiency of our operations but will also promote a sustainable and responsible approach to manufacturing. Regular reviews and updates will ensure that OMI continues to meet industry standards and contribute positively to the environment and community.

**End of Document**

### 14. Employee Development and Training

OMI recognizes the importance of continuous professional development and training for its workforce. By investing in employee skills and capabilities, OMI aims to enhance overall productivity and employee satisfaction while fostering a culture of lifelong learning.

